( element_normal, manual Professional 6.445: corner, edge and interior
  elements. 3x3 quad4 mesh of 2 x 1 cells. The element_normal is the
  normalized sum of the inward node normals of the element nodes; a node
  normal is the normalized sum of the consistent side normals
  (integral N n dA, i.e. length weighted) of its boundary sides.
  Corner element 1: node 1 (1,2)/sqrt5 + node 2 (0,1) + node 5 (1,0) +
  interior node 6 (0,0) -> (1.4472,1.8944)/|.| = (0.60706,0.79465).
  Edge element 2: (0,1); interior element 5: (0,0).
  Values measured on Pro 02-08-2026 (the group with the _automatic
  record contains only element 1: the Professional aborts with an
  assertion when an element with a zero normal uses it). )

echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 2
materi_velocity
materi_displacement
materi_strain_total
materi_stress
end_initia

node 1  0 0
node 2  2 0
node 3  4 0
node 4  6 0
node 5  0 1
node 6  2 1
node 7  4 1
node 8  6 1
node 9  0 2
